#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The RSDRP cannot govern by itself yet. Because we do not have an electoral majority, we need the support of other parties. Recently, our governments have consisted of the Weimar Coalition of the RSDRP, Center, and Democratic parties. We can reach out and build additional connections with these parties, or perhaps we can stand alone.

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the Liberal Müsavat and Kadet Parties.
- @eser: Strengthen our bonds with the Narodist PSR.
- @rkp: Work towards repairing relationships with the Communists and Left Narodists.
- @rsdrp_alone: The RSDRP can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@rkp
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; rkp_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: rkp_blutmai if blutmai = 1; rkp_1 if blutmai = 0 and rkp_coalition_success = 0 and (rkp_relation < 40 or rkp_rectified_history = 1); rkp_rectification_of_history if rkp_relation >= 40 and rkp_rectified_history = 0; rkp_2 if rkp_coalition_success = 1 and rkp_rectified_history = 1

@rkp_1
on-arrival: rkp_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if rkp_inter_party_seen <= 1; reformist_dissent += 2; psr_relation -= 2; kadets_relation -= 3

The Left Esers are suspicious of our overtures, especially their Bolshevik faction, who persist in calling us "petty-bourgeois". However, connections are made at the grassroots and local levels.

@rkp_rectification_of_history

One stumbling block for our relations with the far-left is our history of conflict, dating back to the party split. The PLSRI is especially contemptuous of us for cooperating with the PSR. They also blame us for the deaths of Lenin and Spiridnova, RSDRP and PSR leaders who were killed during the failed Bolshevik revolt.

For further improvements in PLSRI relations, it might be necessary to condemn the army, and hold some sort of commemoration for Lenin and Spiridnova.

- @yes_history: Yes, we must apologize for our past actions.
- @no_history: No, we have no need to apologize.

@yes_history
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 12; reformist_strength -= 2; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 6; left_strength += 5; rkp_rectified_history = 1; psr_relation -= 6; kadets_relation -= 6; musavat_relation -= 4; rkp_relation += 8*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1

As part of normalizing relations with the PLSRI, we have to acknowledge the wrongdoings of our past. We have condemned the army, and have held public commemorations for those killed by troops during the uprisings.

This leads to tensions with the moderates and Economists within our party, and criticism from the conservative and liberal parties.

@no_history
on-arrival: rkp_relation -= 3

We have no need to apologize for the actions of the army and police; it is their fault for launching a violent insurrection and trying to overthrow democracy.


@rkp_2
on-arrival: rkp_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if rkp_inter_party_seen <= 1; reformist_dissent += 2; psr_relation -= 3; kadets_relation -= 3

After the success of the coalition government with the PLSRI, they are much more amenable to us.

@rkp_blutmai
on-arrival: rkp_relation += 3*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent += 1

After the events of *Red Tuesday*, reconciling with the Communists is difficult, if not impossible. Nevertheless, we must try.

@eser
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; psr_relation += 2 if psr_party_leader == "Avksentyev"; psr_left +=1;
go-to: center_op if psr_in_government = 1 and rsdrp_in_government = 0 and chancellor != "Brüning"; center_coalition if rsdrp_in_government = 1 and psr_in_government = 1; center_bruning if chancellor = "Brüning"

@center_op
on-arrival: psr_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the PSR-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@center_coalition
on-arrival: psr_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@center_bruning
on-arrival: psr_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The semi-autocratic and conservative-leaning regime of Savinkov makes building friendly relations difficult, but not impossible.

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; musavat_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)
go-to: kadets_loss

The Kadets have been one of our closest rivals through the course of the Republic, but we are not enemies. Perhaps reaching out to their left-wing of Progressives could help us? Even Müsavat has grown considerable less social-democratic in the past years too.

@kadets_loss
on-arrival: kadets_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

Holding meetings with Müsavat is not unheard of, but is unlikely to go anywhere, especially following the expulsion of their socialist-wing back in 1925. The Kadet's left-wing is happy to hear from us, thankfully. However, given the influence of Müsavat and the Kadets among the other minority- and liberal-leaning parties [? if president == "Hindenburg": and with President Hindenburg ?], it can still be helpful to influence them.

@rsdrp_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
